    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49881.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, you know, if it doesn't cross state borders, we think we're clear of the Comstack Act. So even, even worse case scenario, we think that this will be available. Now that's three years supply, right? What happens after three years? Hopefully the elections can kick in. People will vote, not just women, but men, men care about this issue. This is one of the great, I think misnomers of the politics of this issue that men understand the importance of this privacy, right? To their daughters and their nieces and their wives and their friends. It just And at that point, we hope that people will vote. I think this will happen, actually, if people start to understand the consequences of voting for Republicans this year, is the end of privacy for women, if you want to vote for the Republican Party anywhere, up and down the ticket, doesn't matter what office it is, that is a political party that is under the thumb of those who want to take away this right from women. And that's just a political reality we have to realize.",
